    <string name="settings_ai_help_title">How to configure AI parsing</string>
    <string name="settings_ai_help_body">0. Free mode uses %1$s at no charge and needs no configuration. If it is unavailable, switch to Custom mode and enter your provider and API Key. Custom mode accepts any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.\n\n1. Tap a provider preset to fill its endpoint and default model.\n\n2. Choose a model version from the dropdown. API Keys are stored separately for each preset.\n\n3. Enter the provider API Key and tap Save.\n\n4. On the Add item page, type or dictate a description to extract the item name, location and notes.\n\n5. Batch parsing handles speech pauses and extra commas. You can merge selected results into one record and choose which photos to keep.</string>
    <string name="settings_backup_help_title">📦 Backup and restore guide</string>
    <string name="settings_backup_help_body">📤 Export: tap Export and choose a destination to back up items, photos and successful photo indexes.\n\n📥 Import: tap Import, choose a ZIP backup, then select merge or overwrite. Import failure does not clear existing data first.\n\n🧹 Delete all: Settings offers a two-step local data deletion. System gallery photos, external backups and cloud data are not removed.\n\n💡 Export backups regularly to avoid data loss.</string>
